-- owner standing grant OWNER-STANDING-GRANT-1 asks for a dependency check before any retirement).
-- WHAT WAS FOUND (read 2026-11-04T23:00Z to 2026-11-05T00:00Z on origin/main, live D1, the Cloudflare API and Workers Observability):
--   * Nothing on the account can be deleted today. 20 of the 39 scripts have service-binding or HTTP callers in the fleet graph. The other 19 have no caller beyond a qnfo-ops health-probe binding (or none): fourteen are loops or
--     owner-facing surfaces with an active work claim, an owner client or a standing cadence directive today (personal-companion, q08-signal-engine, qnfo-ai-calibration, qnfo-code-orchestrator, qnfo-github-steward, qnfo-memory-mcp,
--     qnfo-social, qnfo-observability, qnfo-tools-mcp, radar-hub, personal-watch, q08-mind, qnfo-jobsearch, qnfo-youtube-shorts), two carry live duties and fold (qnfo-evolve, qnfo-model-eval), and three are not the fleet's to delete:
--       qnfo-workers  the Workers Builds target of this repository: HTTP 410 stub, its build is the REQUIRED status check "Workers Builds: qnfo-workers" of ruleset require-build (id 26544275), recreated on every push (issue 1000156);
--       voice-stt     OpenAI-style /v1/audio/transcriptions on @cf/openai/whisper-large-v3-turbo behind a bearer token the owner holds, appends transcripts to the owner vault (R2 obsidian-vault Daily/<date>.md); no source in the repo
--                     (deleting it destroys the only copy and the token), 0 inbound edges in the fleet graph, 5250 sampled invocations in 16 days all GET /health 200 from fleet probes and no POST: IDENTITY-BOUND, same verdict as REM-A5 2026-10-26;
--       qnfo-fleet-lee  a wrangler-built agent (src/index.js, ASSETS, CF_API_TOKEN secret) on the custom host lee.qnfo.org, workers.dev disabled on purpose (PRs 6137, 6528), 11 POST in 8 days, census attested on the custom host (PRs 7310, 7321),
--                     being wired into the dashboard /cmd console by a live session: IDENTITY-BOUND (the owner decides whether lee.qnfo.org stays).
--   * worker_count_disagreement = 1 is caused by qnfo-workers alone. It read 0 until 2026-10-31 (registry live), then PR 6033 (METRIC-TRIGGER-4991) made qnfo-ai-calibration probeCompletion flip its registry row to retired on every probe so
--     v_executor_roster would skip it. Issue 1000156 (CENSUS-TOMBSTONE-1) had already named the right design: keep the row retired and teach the census a tombstone class; it was closed on a probe that reads only the registry state.
--     Registering the stub live again would fail the 1000156 contract and reverse a recorded design, so the fix is the census (WORKER-COUNT-1.1, qnfo-fleet-control, held by another session until 2026-11-05T00:54Z).
--   * The transformation program (docs/TRANSFORMATION-PROGRAM.md T3) holds the plan of record for worker_count, five W2 levers (T3.2, T3.3, T3.11, T3.12, T3.13) with no issue and no doer, and W2 never dispatches because the W1 exit needs
--     worker_count <= 32, which only those levers can reach (transformation_runs 699: W1 unmet worker_count 38). Reading each lever against the code shows hidden obstacles (kit refusals, the personal/research separation, a
--     PROTECTED name), recorded in the rows below.
-- WHAT THIS ADDS (no worker is edited here; every file a fold touches is claimed by another session):
--   (1) eight ROADMAP-1 rows with doers: the census tombstone class (code-task, qnfo-fleet-control), two fold-kit folds verified with --dry-run (qnfo-evolve into qnfo-cloud-ops, qnfo-model-eval into qnfo-ai-calibration), and the
--       five plan-of-record levers with their obstacles stated;
--   (2) transformation_levers: five existing W2 levers adopted (status dispatched with the issue id, the loop's own convention), two new levers 16 and 17, so the loop tracks them to closure (backup bak_20261105_worker_count_levers);
--   (3) a dated note on 99923, 100480 and 1000156 (backup bak_20261105_worker_count_notes) and one decision_log row with the per-worker verdicts, so the next session does not repeat the analysis.
-- PREDICTION: worker_count_disagreement 0 within 3 h of the WORKER-COUNT-1.1 deploy; worker_count 39 -> 37 after 1.2 and 1.3 (each folded script is deleted only after its binder is repointed); 32 after the five plan levers; the cap of 30
-- needs two more of: voice-stt, qnfo-fleet-lee (owner), qnfo-pdf, qnfo-github-steward (design first).
-- APPLY-BY: ci
-- DB: qnfo-audit
-- Rollback: UPDATE transformation_levers SET status = (SELECT b.status FROM bak_20261105_worker_count_levers b WHERE b.id = transformation_levers.id), issue_id = (SELECT b.issue_id FROM bak_20261105_worker_count_levers b WHERE b.id = transformation_levers.id), dispatched_at = (SELECT b.dispatched_at FROM bak_20261105_worker_count_levers b WHERE b.id = transformation_levers.id), note = (SELECT b.note FROM bak_20261105_worker_count_levers b WHERE b.id = transformation_levers.id) WHERE id IN (SELECT id FROM bak_20261105_worker_count_levers); DELETE FROM transformation_levers WHERE tp = 3 AND n IN (16, 17) AND key IN ('fold-evolve-into-cloud-ops', 'fold-model-eval-into-calibration'); UPDATE agent_issues SET description = (SELECT b.description FROM bak_20261105_worker_count_notes b WHERE b.id = agent_issues.id) WHERE id IN (SELECT id FROM bak_20261105_worker_count_notes);
-- Rollback note: decision_log is append-only and keeps its row; the eight ROADMAP-1 rows are closed by hand with the reason if the plan is withdrawn.
-- CAUSE-MAPPED: registers no metric.
-- spof-review: adds no worker, cron, D1 trigger, route or credential; it writes issue rows, lever rows and one decision row.

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS bak_20261105_worker_count_levers AS SELECT id, tp, n, status, issue_id, dispatched_at, note FROM transformation_levers WHERE tp = 3 AND n IN (2, 3, 11, 12, 13);
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS bak_20261105_worker_count_notes AS SELECT id, description FROM agent_issues WHERE id IN (99923, 100480, 1000156);

